<title>SWEDEN: Sweden, like UK, Danes, has EMU opt-out - Persson.</title>
<headline>Sweden, like UK, Danes, has EMU opt-out - Persson.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Prime Minister Goran Persson said on Wednesday the decision not to join Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU) from its 1999 start was the political equivalent of Danish and British opt-out clauses.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe our statement is the political equivalent of an 'opt-out,' although legally it may be something different,&quot; Persson told reporters at a seminar.</p>
<p>Britain has an opt-out from a single European currency like Denmark, which has already opted out of monetary union as a result of a binding 1993 referendum.</p>
<p>Sweden has the right to remain outside currency union, Persson said.</p>
<p>&quot;Of course we have the right to remain outside. It is written on the first page of our convergence programme that we have that possibility,&quot; Persson said.</p>
<p>-- Peter Fellman, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1016</p>
</text>
